Aim: To install and configure Jenkins.
Steps to perform
1. Open the Ubuntu terminal.
2. Update the system packages:
   sudo apt update
3. Add the Jenkins repository key and repository as required by your manual, then install Jenkins.
   sudo apt-get install jenkins
4. Start Jenkins and check whether it is running:
   sudo systemctl start jenkins
   sudo systemctl status jenkins
5. Open your browser and enter:
   http://localhost:8080
   
   
   For a cloud server, use the server's reachable address and port 8080 instead.
6. Obtain the Jenkins initial administrator password:
   sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
7. Copy the displayed password and paste it into the Jenkins Unlock screen.
8. Click Install Suggested Plugins.
9. After installation, create the first admin user.
10. Enter Username, Password, Full Name and Email.
11. Click Save and Continue.
12. Configure the Jenkins URL.
13. Click Save and Finish.
14. Open the Jenkins Dashboard.
